  "body": "From the same Makera Z1 user report (2026-11-11). Makera machines cool with **air, M7**. The user built a Z1 machine file in the editor and tried to add M7 air cooling: **\"this was ignored when I saved the profile\"**. They asked to be able to:\n- disable the default (flood) cooling in the editor and swap it for air; or\n- keep both in the profile and choose one per operation.\n\n**What we know from the code (main):**\n- A new machine draft is seeded with `\"coolants\": [{ \"name\": \"Flood\", \"mCode\": \"M8\" }]` (`crates/app/src/machine/draft.rs:91`).\n- `add_coolant` adds a name with **no code** (`draft.rs:147-165`). A coolant whose code is never filled in may then be skipped or dropped. That's likely the \"ignored on save\".\n- `carvera.cps` `coolantCode()` returns the **first `Flood` entry**, else the first entry with a code. So a profile still holding the seeded Flood M8 posts **M8**, even after an Air M7 is added. On a Makera that's the wrong M-code: M8 isn't the air blast.\n- Operations choose `CoolantMode` Off / Flood / Mist / Through tool (`crates/post/src/post/coolant.rs`). There's no **Air** mode, and Flood is the silent default, so an op can't ask for \"air\" by name. The generic posts look the word up in the machine's list and refuse by name when it's missing.\n\n**Fix (sketch; the worker decides the details and records them):**\n1. **The editor** can remove or replace the seeded Flood entry, and an added coolant gets its code entered before it's saved. A save never silently drops a coolant; it's refused by name if one is incomplete.\n2. **An `Air` coolant mode** (or \"air blast\", M7 on Makera), selectable per operation, which the posts resolve from the machine's list like Mist.\n3. **A machine-level default coolant**, so a machine whose only coolant is air defaults new operations to Air, not Flood.\n4. **`carvera.cps`** posts the coolant the operation asked for, not \"first Flood\". If the machine has no matching entry, it's a named refusal, never a wrong M-code.\n\nEffort: high: it changes posted G-code (safety floor).\n\n**Done means:**\n- a machine file with only Air M7 posts M7/M9 for a default operation;\n- a profile edited in the GUI keeps its Air M7 after save and reload;\n- an operation asking for a coolant the machine lacks is refused by name;\n- all pinned.\n",
